WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.200
-I'm so happy to see you
in person.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.300
-It's amazing to be able
to touch you.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.300
-Yeah, you're real.
-Yeah, you're real.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.467
-'Cause we were Zoom friends.
-Yes.

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:10.100
-Yeah, when you came on
the show.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.601
And thank you so much
for being here,

00:00:12.601 --> 00:00:14.400
and congrats on the cover of
"Vogue," by the way.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.300
-Thank you. Wow.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:21.067
You know, I haven't actually
touched a copy.

00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:22.968
-You haven't touched a copy?
-No, I've just seen photos
of it.

00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:25.067
-This is real. It's the first
time you're doing this.

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:27.734
Come on. This is a big moment.
-A huge moment.

00:00:27.734 --> 00:00:29.100
-Yeah.
-The whole thing was just --

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.734
-You look gorgeous on the cover.
-Thank you.

00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:32.667
-And I also like this.

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:36.868
Is this your dad,
and is that grandma?

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:38.701
-It is.
-Yeah, look at that. Come on.

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:39.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:42.434
They got to be in "Vogue"
as well?

00:00:42.434 --> 00:00:44.434
How did they feel?

00:00:44.434 --> 00:00:48.467
-Well, my -- I don't think
my dad or my grandma

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:51.667
understood what was happening.

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:55.100
So, my dad was like, you know,
he came, and then, you know,

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.868
they put him in a suit,
and Ghana's really hot,

00:00:56.868 --> 00:00:58.434
so he was just like --
[ Panting ]

00:00:58.434 --> 00:00:59.834
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:01.167
-At the end, you know,
I was like,

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:03.033
"Dad, so, like,
how did you feel?

00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:04.467
It's 'Vogue.'
It's American 'Vogue.'"

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:06.567
He was like, "Yeah, yeah, yeah.
It's something different."

00:01:06.567 --> 00:01:08.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:10.167
-What?
-Yeah.

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:11.801
-You're in "Vogue," Dad.
-Yeah.

00:01:11.801 --> 00:01:15.267
But now that it's like on the
Internet, my dad is just like

00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:18.234
the whole of my village,
Asikuma, where we're from,

00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:20.067
the whole of the village is
proud.

00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:23.868
My grandma also didn't really
understand until they put on

00:01:23.868 --> 00:01:25.734
her dress,
her Issey Miyake dress.

00:01:25.734 --> 00:01:27.133
They did her hair
and her makeup.

00:01:27.133 --> 00:01:31.467
And she was like, "Oh, I'm
beautiful. I'm beautiful."

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:32.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
And she just kept saying it.

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:34.634
It was so sweet.
-Come on.

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:36.334
-Yeah.

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:40.100
-I think the last time we spoke,
"I May Destroy You" was right --

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.801
coming out, it was brand-new.
-Yes.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:45.667
-And you went on to win two
Emmys and a Peabody Award.

00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:49.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
I mean, it was phenomenal.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:50.901
-Thank you.
-You were phenomenal.

00:01:50.901 --> 00:01:52.534
It was phenomenal.

00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:55.033
Did anyone surprise you that
were fans of the show?

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:58.934
-Yes, well, loads, loads. So,
first, it was the Emmys itself.

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:02.234
And to just sit there and have
so many people that I admire

00:02:02.234 --> 00:02:05.567
come up and say, "Well done."
But then also, the big moment

00:02:05.567 --> 00:02:07.801
was getting home to Atlanta

00:02:07.801 --> 00:02:09.467
where I was filming
"Black Panther."

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:12.934
And I entered my house, and
there was a huge bouquet of

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:15.634
white flowers and the note said,

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:17.868
"Proud of you, B.X."

00:02:17.868 --> 00:02:19.067
Beyoncé.

00:02:19.067 --> 00:02:21.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:21.467 --> 00:02:23.601
-Now, have you ever met Beyoncé?

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:27.100
-I've never met Beyoncé.
I've never spoken to Beyoncé.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:29.801
So for her to do that
was slightly insane.

00:02:29.801 --> 00:02:33.334
I've spent my career sort of
like paying homage to her.

00:02:33.334 --> 00:02:35.868
"Chewing Gum Dreams."
"Chewing Gum," sorry --

00:02:35.868 --> 00:02:38.968
There's a photo of Beyoncé
next to Jesus Christ that

00:02:38.968 --> 00:02:40.834
the central character prays to.
-Yeah.

00:02:40.834 --> 00:02:44.267
-I've written articles about
Beyoncé for The Guardian,

00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:47.033
but I've never met her, so for
her to do that meant a lot.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.167
And then she released
"Renaissance."

00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:51.767
-It's fantastic.
-Which was an album and a half.

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:53.501
-It was unbelievable.
-Yes.

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:56.767
And so I sent her a huge plant
and said thank you.

00:02:56.767 --> 00:02:58.601
-You sent her a plant?
-I did, yes.

00:02:58.601 --> 00:03:01.734
-So you kind of talk to
each other through plants.

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:03.868
-Through plants, yeah.
And just through the air

00:03:03.868 --> 00:03:05.501
'cause I don't know
how she got my address.

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:07.300
-Because she's Beyoncé.
-Because she's Beyoncé.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:09.033
-She's magic.
-God knows where you live.

00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:11.634
-Yeah, she's a class act.
Good for you, Beyoncé.

00:03:11.634 --> 00:03:13.701
I love that she did that.
That's awesome.

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:14.934
Can we talk about
"Black Panther?"

00:03:14.934 --> 00:03:17.067
-Yeah.
-Congratulations.

00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:19.934
It's such a big movie.
Are you so excited about this?

00:03:19.934 --> 00:03:24.334
-I'm excited and humbled
and overwhelmed.

00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:28.834
I think, obviously Chadwick
passed, and it meant that there

00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:32.901
was this sort of gaping hole
and a lot of grief in the hearts

00:03:32.901 --> 00:03:34.901
of the cast as well as joy.
-Yeah.

00:03:34.901 --> 00:03:37.767
-So it just feels --
the emotions are complex.

00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:40.334
It's not just, "Oh, I'm excited,
I'm in 'Black Panther.'"

00:03:40.334 --> 00:03:43.033
It just feels weighty.
-It's a moment.

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:46.534
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
But I'm honored to have been

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:48.701
there to support the cast.

00:03:48.701 --> 00:03:50.734
-In every article that I read
about you,

00:03:50.734 --> 00:03:52.167
about this upcoming movie,
you said,

00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:54.601
"I want to set it straight.
I am not the next --"

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:55.901
-Yes.
-"The new Black Panther."

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:58.834
-Yes. I have to keep minimizing
expectations

00:03:58.834 --> 00:04:00.968
for the people that,
like, love me.

00:04:00.968 --> 00:04:03.167
-Yes.
-Minimize expectations about

00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:05.667
how much I'm in the movie.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:09.367
You know, I'm there. I'm there,
but I'm not, like, panthering.

00:04:09.367 --> 00:04:12.033
-Okay, you're not doing --
No, no, you're not panthering.

00:04:12.033 --> 00:04:13.934
-No, no, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.934 --> 00:04:15.567
-You're not panthering at all.
Yeah, no.

00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:18.200
But this is interesting.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.801
You auditioned for the first
"Black Panther."

00:04:20.801 --> 00:04:23.534
-I did.
-And didn't get the part.

00:04:23.534 --> 00:04:26.534
-Correct.
I auditioned in like 2012,

00:04:26.534 --> 00:04:29.834
I think, when I first left
drama school.

00:04:29.834 --> 00:04:34.467
And it was a tape, you know, and
it was probably a very bad tape.

00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:38.534
I'd never been on TV.
I'd never been in any film.

00:04:38.534 --> 00:04:41.801
So I think I was probably one of
like thousands

00:04:41.801 --> 00:04:44.868
of people trying to get a part.

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:47.968
I think -- I think a part
very similar to mine.

00:04:47.968 --> 00:04:50.567
-To who you play.
Yeah, you can say who you --

00:04:50.567 --> 00:04:51.634
-Yeah, everyone knows that.

00:04:51.634 --> 00:04:53.400
-Do they?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:54.868
-There's Marvel people
in the audience.

00:04:54.868 --> 00:04:56.067
They're like,
"Don't you say that!"

00:04:56.067 --> 00:04:58.200
-Yes. Yes, they're very
Fort Knox on everything.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:59.434
-Well, we're going to show
a clip.

00:04:59.434 --> 00:05:01.234
-Exactly.

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:02.634
-We're allowed to
speak about it. Yeah.

00:05:02.634 --> 00:05:04.267
-Yes, exactly.
-This is going to be big.

00:05:04.267 --> 00:05:06.033
I'm so happy to see you
in person.

00:05:06.033 --> 00:05:07.767
You're just as cool as I thought
you'd be.

00:05:07.767 --> 00:05:09.434
-You too, Jimmy.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:05:09.434 --> 00:05:10.834
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:10.834 --> 00:05:13.334
Here's Michaela Coel in "Black
Panther: Wakanda Forever."

00:05:13.334 --> 00:05:14.667
Take a look at this.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:20.801 --> 00:05:23.267
-Aneka, where is your spear?

00:05:23.267 --> 00:05:24.767
-Shuri gave me these to try.

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:29.067
You know, I like them better.

00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:30.767
-Our foremothers gave us
this spear

00:05:30.767 --> 00:05:36.133
because it is precise, elegant,
and deadly.

00:05:39.033 --> 00:05:43.334
It will not change
under my watch.

00:05:43.334 --> 00:05:45.601
-Yes, General.

00:05:45.601 --> 00:05:47.601
-I told you not to bring them.

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:53.634
-Oh, come on now.

00:05:53.634 --> 00:05:55.767
Michaela Coel, everybody.

00:05:55.767 --> 00:05:57.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:57.634 --> 00:06:00.167
"Black Panther: Wakanda Forever"
is in theaters

00:06:00.167 --> 00:06:02.334
and IMAX November 11th.

00:06:02.334 --> 00:06:05.634
Zedd and Maren Morris perform
for us after the break.

00:06:05.634 --> 00:06:07.634
Stick around, everybody.
Come on back.

